  "notes": "Every number here comes from training documents only, or from counts of positions, and is written before any held-out number for this checkpoint exists. All randomness streams from base seed 0, which the committed gate record fixes in its third answer of record. The readout chosen by this cross-validation is recorded and is not this checkpoint's chosen readout: the design chooses that on held-out documents, immediately below. The window's low end can sit above 1, because the first column of a line needs a one-character opening token and is thin; how far above is recorded. The four profile parts are fixed by the design at 1 to 35, 36 to 70, 71 to 105 and 106 to 140. The selected best readout and the selected ridge strength are logged beside the pooled quality and the boundary ratio, and a selection sitting at an end of its search range is flagged. The ends are readout 0, readout 24, strength 1 and strength 100000. The previous rung's committed gate record adopts this control as binding and this rung's design carries it forward. Both state in advance that the initialization checkpoint is expected to trip it, because a random model has no meaningful best readout: on the smaller sibling it selected readout 24 at strength 10000. There the flag is confirmation, not alarm. A further run of this script on the same box is a rerun of the same instrument, not a replication.",
